step Expert Leatherworking
  zone Azeroth
  tip Expert raises the cap from 150 to 225; it needs Leatherworking 125 and character level 20, so you can take it on any visit from 125. Only a few trainers teach it: Alliance Drakk Stonehand (The Hinterlands) and Telonis (Darnassus); Horde Hahrana Ironhide (Feralas) and Una (Thunder Bluff). The arrow picks the nearest of your faction. 150-225 takes about 1g 68s of vendor goods, plus 257 Thick Leather to gather or buy. Come with all of it in your bags (the steps above, the rest from the Auction House): these trainers also teach Thick Leather (from 155) and Thick Armor Kit (from 175), and the crafts need no station, so craft right here and learn each recipe as you reach its skill. One trip instead of 3. Rugged Leather (from 205) takes a second trip, to other trainers (below).
  level 20
  train Leatherworking Expert

step Heavy Armor Kit to 155
  tip Heavy Armor Kit is yellow at 150 (yellow 145, green 155, grey 165): about 8 crafts to 155. Each takes 5 Heavy Leather and 1 Fine Thread. Five Heavy Leather a craft (beasts of level 28-40); the kits sell to vendors.
  craft 3780 until 155

step Leatherworking recipes at 155
  tip Still at the Expert trainer: Thick Leather (from 155).
  learn 20650

step Thick Leather to 177
  tip Thick Leather is orange at 155 (yellow 175, green 177, grey 180): about 23 crafts to 177. Each takes 6 Heavy Leather. Six Heavy Leather make one Thick Leather, orange until 175: keep them, the Thick Armor Kits next use them.
  craft 20650 until 177

step Leatherworking recipes at 177
  tip Still at the Expert trainer: Thick Armor Kit (from 175).
  learn 10487

step Thick Armor Kit to 205
  tip Thick Armor Kit is orange at 177 (yellow 195, green 205, grey 215): about 32 crafts to 205. Each takes 5 Thick Leather and 1 Silken Thread. Use the 23 Thick Leather you made earlier; the counts above leave them out. Five Thick Leather a craft; the kits sell to vendors.
  craft 10487 until 205

step Leatherworking recipes at 205
  tip Rugged Leather (from 205) is taught only by the Artisan trainers: Alliance Drakk Stonehand (The Hinterlands); Horde Hahrana Ironhide (Feralas). You can train Artisan there now if you are level 35 (it needs Leatherworking 200), which saves the trip at 225.
  learn 22331 npc 11097 only Alliance map 1425
  learn 22331 npc 11098 only Horde
  train Leatherworking Artisan optional

step Rugged Leather to 225
  tip Rugged Leather is orange at 205 (yellow 225, green 225, grey 225): about 20 crafts to 225, a point every craft. Each takes 6 Thick Leather. Rugged Leather from Thick Leather: the points come cheap and you need the Rugged Leather next. Leatherworking 225 is a Legacy System milestone.
  craft 22331 until 225
  skill Leatherworking 225

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Artisan (225-300)

step Artisan Leatherworking
  tip Artisan raises the cap from 225 to 300; it needs Leatherworking 200 and character level 35, so you can take it on any visit from 200. Only a few trainers teach it: Alliance Drakk Stonehand (The Hinterlands); Horde Hahrana Ironhide (Feralas). The arrow picks the nearest of your faction. Learn now: Rugged Armor Kit (from 205). 225-300 takes about 3g 40s of recipes and 44g 90s of vendor goods, plus 1009 Rugged Leather and 430 Runecloth to gather or buy.
  level 35
  train Leatherworking Artisan
  learn 19058

step Leatherworking 225-300: vendor goods
